<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cfsSimulation xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation ../../../../../share/xml/CFS-Simulation/CFS.xsd"
               xmlns="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation">

  <documentation>
    <title>Contact across NON-MATCHING interface meshes</title>
    <authors><author>kroppert</author></authors>
    <date>2026-08-06</date>
    <keywords><keyword>contact</keyword></keywords>
    <references>none</references>
    <isVerified>no</isVerified>
    <description>
      Two stacked 2D plane-strain blocks with DIFFERENT interface discretizations: the lower
      body is split into two elements, the upper into one. The single secondary element
      therefore STRADDLES the primary element boundary at x = 0, and its two Gauss points
      project onto two different primary elements.

      That is the configuration that exposed a silent correctness bug. The assembler element
      list used to hold one entry per secondary element, whose ptPrimary was taken from the
      first projected point; SurfaceBiLinFormContext::MapEqns() then handed out THAT primary
      element's equation numbers for the whole element matrix, while the integrator evaluated
      each point on its own primary element. The primary-side contribution of the second point
      was written into the first element's equations. The solve still converged to machine
      precision -- on a wrong system, with the contact force off by a factor of 80 and no
      warning of any kind.

      Load transfer is the check that cannot be fooled: whatever the meshes, the interface is
      the only load path to the support, so the resultant contact force must equal the applied
      one exactly.
    </description>
  </documentation>

  <fileFormats>
    <input>
      <hdf5 fileName="ContactNonMatching2d.h5" linearizeEntities="__none__"/>
    </input>
    <output><hdf5/></output>
    <materialData file="mat.xml" format="xml"/>
  </fileFormats>

  <domain geometryType="plane">
    <regionList>
      <region name="master_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
      <region name="slave_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
    </regionList>
    <surfRegionList>
      <surfRegion name="master_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="slave_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="top"/>
      <surfRegion name="bottom"/>
    </surfRegionList>
  </domain>

  <fePolynomialList>
    <Lagrange><gridOrder/></Lagrange>
  </fePolynomialList>

  <integrationSchemeList>
    <scheme>
      <method>Gauss</method>
      <order>4</order>
      <mode>absolute</mode>
    </scheme>
  </integrationSchemeList>

  <sequenceStep>
    <analysis><static/></analysis>

    <pdeList>
      <mechanic subType="planeStrain">
        <regionList>
          <region name="master_elem"/>
          <region name="slave_elem"/>
        </regionList>

        <contactList>
          <contactPair name="nonmatching_contact"
                       primarySurface="master_iface"
                       secondarySurface="slave_iface"
                       slidingType="small"
                       normalPenalty="100"
                       initialGapHandling="fromMesh"
                       integrationOrder="2"/>
        </contactList>

        <bcsAndLoads>
          <!-- lower body fully supported -->
          <fix name="bottom">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- upper body: suppress the lateral rigid-body mode only. Its y support comes
               exclusively from the contact interface, which is the point of the test. -->
          <fix name="top">
            <comp dof="x"/>
          </fix>
          <pressure name="top" value="1e6"/>
        </bcsAndLoads>

        <storeResults>
          <nodeResult type="mechDisplacement"><allRegions/></nodeResult>
        </storeResults>
      </mechanic>
    </pdeList>

    <linearSystems>
      <system>
        <solutionStrategy>
          <standard>
            <setup idbcHandling="penalty"/>
            <matrix storage="sparseNonSym" reordering="noReordering"/>
            <nonLinear method="newton" logging="no">
              <lineSearch type="none"/>
              <incStopCrit>1e-9</incStopCrit>
              <resStopCrit>1e-9</resStopCrit>
              <maxNumIters>20</maxNumIters>
            </nonLinear>
          </standard>
        </solutionStrategy>
        <solverList><directLU/></solverList>
      </system>
    </linearSystems>

  </sequenceStep>
</cfsSimulation>
